config PWM_LOONGSON_LS_TIMER
	bool "Loongson 2K0300 ATIM/GTIM PWM driver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_LOONGSON_LS2K_PWM_TIMER_ENABLED
	help
	  Enable the PWM front end of the Loongson 2K0300 ATIM/GTIM timer blocks.
	  The driver is bound to the "loongson,ls2k-pwm-timer" child node of a
	  "loongson,loongson-timers" block, which is how the vendor device tree
	  and Linux describe it (drivers/mfd/loongson-timers.c plus
	  drivers/pwm/pwm-ls-timer.c); registers, clock and pinctrl are taken from
	  that parent node.

	  The number of channels and the width of the auto reload register are
	  probed at run time. Capture, break inputs and the complementary outputs
	  of the ATIM are not implemented.
